diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 12b32a31..ef843312 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@ Initial release of nf-core/scdownstream, created with the [nf-core](https://nf-c
 
 ### `Added`
 
+- Accept custom CellTypist model files (local paths or URLs ending in `.pkl`) in `--celltypist_model`, alongside model names ([#213](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/issues/213)) by @kroy3 [[#384](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/384)].
 - Add opt-in pathway and transcription factor activity analysis with decoupler (`--decoupler`), scoring pseudobulk profiles and pseudobulk DE contrasts with PROGENy, CollecTRI, MSigDB Hallmark or a custom network (`decoupler/network`, `decoupler/activity`, `decoupler/enrichment`, `decoupler` subworkflow), by @nictru and Cursor [[#321](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/321)].
 - Add EmptyDrops from DropletUtils as an alternative empty droplet removal method, selectable with `--empty_droplet_removal emptydrops` and tuned via `--emptydrops_lower` and `--emptydrops_fdr` ([#169](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/issues/169)) by @nictru and Cursor [[#322](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/322)].
 - Add opt-in `--tords` to convert the final AnnData object to RDS via `ADATA_TORDS` (off by default) by @nictru [[#308](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/308)].
diff --git a/docs/usage.md b/docs/usage.md
index 2712fd57..1997ebdc 100644
--- a/docs/usage.md
+++ b/docs/usage.md
@@ -200,6 +200,8 @@ The pipeline supports automated cell type annotation with [Celltypist](https://g
 
 [Celltypist](https://github.com/Teichlab/celltypist) annotates cells using pretrained logistic regression models. Specify the models with [`celltypist_model`](https://nf-co.re/scdownstream/dev/parameters/#celltypist_model); use a comma-separated list for multiple models. Available models are listed on the [Celltypist models page](https://www.celltypist.org/models). When this parameter is empty (the default), Celltypist is skipped.
 
+You can also use custom or pre-downloaded models by giving the path or URL of a `.pkl` model file in place of a name, for example `--celltypist_model Immune_All_Low,/path/to/my_model.pkl`. Entries ending in `.pkl` are staged and loaded directly; all other entries are downloaded by name. The file name without the `.pkl` extension becomes the model name in the output columns (e.g. `annotation:celltypist:my_model:per_cell`), so every model must end up with a unique name. The pipeline fails if two entries resolve to the same name.
+
 #### singleR
 
 For `singleR`, you can provide a CSV file with information about the celldex references to use for the singleR cell type annotation with the [`celldex_reference` parameter](https://nf-co.re/scdownstream/dev/parameters/#celldex_reference).
